The Quarter
A title sequence for the Atlanta Design Festival's Industry Resources, made entirely in code.
No stock footage, no generated video, no generated images, no photographs.

TYPEFACES
  League Gothic — The League of Moveable Type — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Used for the credits, which are the sets: the role list, the site names, the figures.
  League Spartan — The League of Moveable Type — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Used for the subtitle strip.
  Licence texts ship beside the fonts in fonts/.
  The title lettering (THE QUARTER) is drawn for this film in cuttitle.js: geometric paper-cut
  letterforms, straight cuts and arcs, with uneven weights and a staggered baseline. It is not
  based on any existing title's lettering, logo or mark.

ENGINE
  The paper-cut engine (paper.js, glyph.js, chars.js) comes from the Lemo-Opuscar library's
  60s Spy Title Sequence demo and is used as the technical base this style ships for the purpose:
  scissor-cut edges cached in local space, cut gaps, paper shadows, the paper texture and the
  silhouette layer with joint slits. github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, code MIT. The four inks,
  the story, the sets, the staging, the title lettering, the score and the timing are this film's
  own; none of the demo's story, shots, props or timings are in it. The demo's brass key is
  explicitly not carried over: this courier carries the sponsor's package.

  opentype.js 1.3.4 (MIT) reads the font outlines so each letter can be re-cut.

SOUND
  Score and foley synthesised in this project (mix.py) with numpy and scipy: stacked brass,
  crash, walking upright bass, surf-guitar twang through a spring reverb, brushes, bongos,
  shaker, vibraphone, flute and organ, and the paper and tape foley. An original motif in D minor
  at 144 BPM. No sample libraries, no recordings, no third-party audio. The score deliberately
  avoids the chromatic figure and the ending chord of the best-known spy theme.

VOICE
  Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice am_michael, run locally and offline, then put through a tape chain
  in mix.py: band-pass 220-5200 Hz, soft saturation, slow wow and hiss. Synthetic narration, not a
  recording of a person. Script in lines.json, subtitles in the .srt.

  The speech-to-text check the pipeline normally runs could not run here: the Whisper model host
  is unreachable from this environment. The six lines carry no digits or abbreviations, and the
  subtitles carry the authoritative wording.

CONTENT
  Every figure is from the client's own Industry Resources 2027 kit: 8,911 industry subscribers,
  39% average open, 19% average click, 0.2% unsubscribe, three sites, four slots a year, and the
  2027 founding rate of $2,500 which the kit states rises to $5,000 for 2028. The film quotes
  rates and the published inventory; it promises no reach, because the kit's own performance line
  is an average of past editions rather than a guarantee.

